The '''2026 Redbridge London Borough Council election''' will take place on 7 May 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-01 |title=Local elections in London will test support for Reform UK and Greens |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c99k0mzj7x8o |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> All 63 members of [[Redbridge London Borough Council]] will be elected. The elections will take place alongside [[2026 London local elections|local elections in the other London boroughs]] and [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|elections to local authorities across the United Kingdom]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Number of councils that have requested delay to local elections revealed - is yours one of them? |url=https://news.sky.com/story/local-elections-2026-over-a-third-of-councils-offered-a-delay-have-requested-one-is-yours-on-the-list-13494762 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Sky News |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
Redbridge Council has historically swung between [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] control and periods of no overall control, until the [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] won its first majority in 2014.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Elgueta |first=Adriana |date=2026-04-07 |title=Local elections 2026: Redbridge borough facts and analysis |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq8w04v5ek9o |access-date=2026-04-07 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>

