Changes 2022–2026:
*November 2022: Kabir Mahmud (Labour) leaves party to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite web |last1=Boothroyd |first1=David |title=Noted for fresh air and fun |url=https://www.localcouncils.co.uk/2022/11/noted-for-fresh-air-and-fun/ |website=LocalCouncils.co.uk}}</ref>
*February 2024: Shanelle Johnson (Labour) leaves party to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mellor |first1=Josh |title=Redbridge councillor left the Labour Party with a scathing criticism of leader Jas Athwal’s “top-down leadership approach” - Asian Standard Newspaper |url=https://www.asianstandard.co.uk/redbridge-councillor-left-the-labour-party-with-a-scathing-criticism-of-leader-jas-athwals-top-down-leadership-approach/ |access-date=21 January 2026 |work=Asian Standard |date=1 February 2024}}</ref>
*June 2024: Rosa Gomez (Labour) leaves party to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mann |first1=Sebastian |title=Redbridge Labour councillor quits party over claims she ‘felt like outsider’ - Asian Standard Newspaper |url=https://www.asianstandard.co.uk/redbridge-labour-councillor-quits-party-over-claims-she-felt-like-outsider/ |access-date=21 January 2026 |work=Asian Standard |date=12 June 2024}}</ref>
*October 2024: [[Bayo Alaba]] (Labour) resigns – by-election held November 2024<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mann |first1=Sebastian |title=Newly-elected MP's resignation as councillor triggers by-election |url=https://www.ilfordrecorder.co.uk/news/24660954.bayo-alaba-resignation-wanstead-councillor-triggers-vote/ |access-date=21 January 2026 |work=Ilford Recorder |date=18 October 2024 |language=en}}</ref>
*November 2024: Emma Shepherd-Mallinson (Labour) wins by-election<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Wanstead Park Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/19465/#2024-11-14 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=21 January 2026}}</ref>
*February 2025: [[Jas Athwal]] (Labour) resigns – by-election held March 2025<ref>{{cite news |title=Jas Athwal: Labour MP stands down as Redbridge councillor |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cevxgl147lgo |access-date=21 January 2026 |work=BBC News |date=24 February 2025}}</ref>
*March 2025: 
**Noor Begum (Ilford Independents) gains by-election from Labour<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Mayfield Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/19459/#2025-03-27 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=21 January 2026}}</ref>
**Sam Gould (Labour) suspended from party and resigns – by-election held May 2025<ref>{{cite news |title=Wes Streeting ex-aide Sam Gould resigns as Redbridge councillor |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c78exj07w09o |access-date=21 January 2026 |work=BBC News |date=14 March 2025}}</ref>
*May 2025: Helen Mullis (Labour) wins by-election<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Hainault Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/19456/#2025-05-01 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=21 January 2026}}</ref>
*March 2026: Rosa Gomez (Independent) disqualified for non-attendance – seat left vacant until 2026 election<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mann |first1=Sebastian |title=Disabled councillor dismissed over non-attendance blames Redbridge's 'failure to meet needs' |url=https://www.yellowad.co.uk/disabled-councillor-dismissed-over-non-attendance-blames-redbridges-failure-to-meet-needs/ |access-date=5 May 2026 |work=Yellow Advertiser |date=10 March 2026}}</ref>
*April 2026: Hannah Chaudhry (Labour) resigns – seat left vacant until 2026 election<ref>{{cite web |last1=Boothroyd |first1=David |title=Reform councillor wafted here from paradise |url=https://www.localcouncils.co.uk/2026/04/reform-councillor-wafted-here-from-paradise/ |website=LocalCouncils.co.uk |access-date=5 May 2026}}</ref>

